      "writtenOn": "2022-10-25T16:03:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dang, I wish we could IWYU annotate the template instead. Doing this means that `SkSpan.h` is publicly providing all of `\u003ctype_traits\u003e` so anything that includes `SkSpan.h` won\u0027t need to include `\u003ctype_traits\u003e` if they\u0027re using other type traits. This is a really big hammer that kinda breaks using IWYU. In some sense not using IWYU is like \"exporting\" all includes, so it\u0027s not totally broken or anything, but in this case `SkSpan.h` really doesn\u0027t want to publicly export this. On the other hand this is worse because not IWYU can either remove `\u003ctype_traits\u003e` includes or not suggest them when it should.",
      "revId": "545b3a747d35847c26cca658e5f7d1cdb27c6eca",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e7056f15_981377e2",
        "filename": "include/core/SkSpan.h",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-25T17:17:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This was added because of a complaint about a lot of churn with respect to this include. At least in IWYU 0.17, it would suggest the addition and removal of this a lot, seemingly randomly. Maybe that\u0027s not the case in 0.19, but I figured I would like our tools to not be frustrating, at the cost of not being perfect.",
      "parentUuid": "257d2742_0120c9d9",
      "revId": "545b3a747d35847c26cca658e5f7d1cdb27c6eca",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
